# ParachuteComputer workspace meta-repo
#
# Strategy: ignore everything by default; allowlist what we want tracked.
# This is a workspace container — every sibling repo here (parachute-*) is
# its own git repo. We track only workspace-level orchestration: the
# CLAUDE.md, the custom .claude/ skills/agents, workspace docs, scratch
# session-state notes.

# ── Default: ignore everything ──
*

# ── Allowlist: workspace meta files ──
!.gitignore
!CLAUDE.md
!README.md

# ── Allowlist: workspace docs ──
!docs/
!docs/**

# ── Within docs/: the historical bin stays LOCAL-ONLY ──
# docs/historical/ holds pre-vault-era root artifacts (DESIGN-*, HANDOFF-*,
# client notes, launch docs) that were never committed — this repo is PUBLIC,
# and they contain private/internal material. Only the README (which explains
# the bin) is tracked. Mine them into the team vault, don't publish them.
docs/historical/*
!docs/historical/README.md

# ── Allowlist: workspace-wide tooling ──
# audit-canonical-refs.sh etc. — moved here from parachute-patterns (2026-07-04).
!scripts/
!scripts/**

# ── Allowlist: scratch session notes ──
# Handoffs, process audits, thinking docs. Tracked because they're
# knowledge about how we work, not ephemeral state.
!scratch/
!scratch/**

# ── Allowlist: the e2e video harness ──
# Containerised browser stack that records a video of a change working end to
# end. Lives at workspace level rather than in a module repo because the stack
# spans vault + app, and "a PR arrives with a video" is a workspace practice.
!e2e/
!e2e/**

# ── Within e2e/: run output is never tracked ──
# Videos, traces, screenshots and the HTML report are regenerated every run and
# run to tens of MB. The artifact belongs attached to a PR, not in history.
e2e/artifacts/
e2e/node_modules/
e2e/package-lock.json

# ── Allowlist: .claude/ workspace customization ──
# Custom agents, slash commands, workspace-level settings.
# NOT user-level state (history, cache, etc. — those live in ~/.claude/).
!.claude/
!.claude/**

# ── Within .claude/: explicit per-file ignores ──
# settings.local.json contains operator-local paths (different per machine);
# track a settings.json template instead and let each operator override.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/cache/
.claude/history*

# ── Sub-repos (every parachute-*, plus exploration repos) ──
# Each is its own git repo with its own .git/. Ignoring at this level
# means git status doesn't recurse into them. They're not tracked, not
# submodules — they're parallel checkouts coordinated by convention.
# (No explicit listing needed since `*` already ignores them.)

# ── Operator-local ──
# Anything starting with a dot at the root that isn't allowlisted above
# is ignored. This includes .DS_Store, editor state, etc.
